{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-74-1","title":"Psalms 74:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The prophet complains of the desolation of the sanctuary. 10 He moves God to help in consideration of his power; 18 of his reproachful enemies, of his children, and of his covenant.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3416. B.C. 588. (Title.) Maschil of Asaph. or, APsalm for Asaph to give instruction. 78:1; *title O God. 10:1; 42:9,11; 44:9; 60:1,10; 77:7; Jer 31:37; 33:24-26; Ro 11:1,2 smoke. 79:5; De 29:20 the sheep. 79:13; 95:7; 100:3; Jer 23:1; Eze 34:8,31; Lu 12:32; Joh 10:26-30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-2","title":"Psalms 74:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>purchased. Ex 15:16; De 9:29; Ac 20:28 rod. or, tribe. thine. 33:12; 106:40; 135:4; De 4:20; 32:9; Jer 10:16 redeemed. Isa 51:11; 62:12; Tit 2:14; Re 5:9 this mount. 48:1,2; 78:68,69; 132:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-3","title":"Psalms 74:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Lift. 44:23,26; Jos 10:24; 2Sa 22:39-43; Isa 10:6; 25:10; 63:3-6; Mic 1:3 the perpetual. 102:13,14; Ne 1:3; 2:3,13; Isa 64:10,11; Da 9:17; Mic 3:12 Lu 21:24; Re 11:2 all. 79:1; Jer 52:13; La 1:10; Da 8:11-14; 9:27; 11:31; Mr 11:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-4","title":"Psalms 74:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Thine. 2Ch 36:17; La 2:7; Lu 13:1; Re 13:6 they set. Jer 6:1-5; Da 6:27; Mt 24:15; Lu 21:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-5","title":"Psalms 74:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>1Ki 5:6; 2Ch 2:14; Jer 46:22,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-6","title":"Psalms 74:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>1Ki 6:18,29,32,35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-7","title":"Psalms 74:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>cast fire into thy sanctuary. Heb. sent thy sanctuary intothe fire. 2Ki 25:9; Isa 64:11; Mt 22:7 defiled. 89:39; Eze 24:21 dwelling. Ex 20:24; De 12:5; 1Ki 8:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-8","title":"Psalms 74:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>said. 83:4; 137:7; Es 3:8,9 destroy. Heb. break. all the synagogues. 2Ki 2:3,5; 4:23; 2Ch 17:9; Mt 4:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-9","title":"Psalms 74:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>We see. Ex 12:13; 13:9,10; Jud 6:17; Eze 20:12; Heb 2:4 no more. 1Sa 3:1; Am 8:11; Mic 3:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-10","title":"Psalms 74:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>13:1,2; 79:4,5; 89:46,50,51; Da 12:6; Re 6:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-11","title":"Psalms 74:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>withdrawest. Isa 64:12; La 2:3 pluck it out.As the outward habit of the easterns has no sleeves, the hands and arms are frequently covered with the folds of the robe; and, in order to do anything, the hand must be disentangled, and drawn out.</p>\n<p>44:23; 78:65,66</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-12","title":"Psalms 74:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>God. 44:4; Ex 19:5,6; Nu 23:21,22; Isa 33:22 working. Ex 15:2-15; Jud 4:23,24; 1Sa 19:5; Isa 63:8; Hab 3:12-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-13","title":"Psalms 74:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>divide. Heb. break. 66:6; 78:13; 106:8,9; 136:13-18; Ex 14:21; Ne 9:11; Isa 11:15,16 brakest. Ex 14:28; Isa 51:9,10; Eze 29:3 dragons. or, whales. Eze 32:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-14","title":"Psalms 74:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>leviathan. 104:25,26; Job 3:8; *marg: Job 41:1-34; Isa 27:1; Re 20:2 meat. 72:9; Ex 12:35,36; 14:30; Nu 14:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-15","title":"Psalms 74:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>cleave. 105:41; Ex 17:5,6; Nu 20:11; Isa 48:21 flood. Jos 3:13-17; 2Ki 2:8,14; Isa 11:16; 44:27; Hab 3:9; *marg: Re 16:12 mighty rivers. Heb. rivers of strength.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-16","title":"Psalms 74:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>The day. 136:7-9; Ge 1:3-5 prepared. 8:3; 19:1-6; 136:7-9; Ge 1:14-18; Mt 5:45</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-17","title":"Psalms 74:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>set. 24:1,2; De 32:8; Ac 17:26 made summer. Heb. made them summer. Ge 8:22; Ac 14:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-18","title":"Psalms 74:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Remember. 22; 89:50,51; 137:7; Isa 62:6,7; *marg: Re 16:19 the foolish. 41:1; 39:8; 94:2-8; De 32:27; Isa 37:23,24; Eze 20:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-19","title":"Psalms 74:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>turtle-dove. 68:13; So 2:14; 4:1; 6:9; Isa 60:8; Mt 10:16 forget. 68:10; 72:2; Zep 3:12; Jas 2:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-20","title":"Psalms 74:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Have. 89:28,34-36,39; 105:8; 106:45; Ge 17:7,8; Ex 24:6-8; Le 26:40-45 De 9:27; 2Sa 23:5; Jer 33:20-26; Lu 1:72-75; Heb 8:10 the dark. De 12:31; Ro 1:29-31; Eph 4:17,18 habitations. 5:8; Ge 49:5-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-21","title":"Psalms 74:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>O let not. 9:18; 12:5; 102:19-21; 109:22; Isa 45:17 poor. 102:21; Ezr 3:11; Jer 33:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-22","title":"Psalms 74:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Arise. 9:19,20; 79:9,10 remember. 18; 75:4,5; 89:50,51; Isa 52:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-74-23","title":"Psalms 74:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":74,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":74,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Forget. 10:11,12; 13:1 tumult. 4; 2:1,2; Isa 37:29; La 2:16; Re 17:14 increaseth. Heb. ascendeth. Jon 1:2</p>"}]}